From 12e44977c650ec7e78d7cfd5185833f382a68f9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Curley <rebe@kixel.us>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:26:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(common): seal AES-256-GCM payloads and stream-key
 envelopes with rind

Client-side AES-256-GCM encryption and the stream-key envelope now use
rind's AES-256-GCM instead of RustCrypto's aes-gcm. The wire format is
unchanged: tests check that payloads and envelopes sealed by aes-gcm open
under the new code and the other way round. aes-gcm stays a dev-dependency
for those tests and for the stream_encryption bench's raw comparison.
AES-256-GCM-SIV stays on aes-gcm-siv.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
